  "title": "Erdős Problem #1129",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "For $x_1,\\ldots,x_n\\in [-1,1]$ let $ l_k(x)=\\frac{\\prod_{i\neq k}(x-x_i)}{\\prod_{i\neq k}(x_k-x_i)}, $ which are such that $l_k(x_k)=1$ and $l_k(x_i)=0$ for $i\neq k$.\nDescribe which choice of $x_i$ minimise $ \\Lambda(x_1,\\ldots,x_n)=\\max_{x\\in [-1,1]} \\sum_k \\lvert l_k(x)\\rvert. $ ",
